- id: typical-workflow
  title: Composition Workflow
  audience: all
  summary: Create patterns, assign channels, apply harmony and arrange song slots.
  prose: '1. Configure one output and create a short pattern.

    2. Assign the pattern to a channel.

    3. Select and apply a scale.

    4. Add melody using masks or MIDI recording.

    5. Apply velocity changes or parameter locks.

    6. Copy the sequence into song slots and edit each variation.

    7. Save a named project.


    Patterns supply musical material. Channels combine that material and apply exceptions. Song slots
    store sequence variations. See [Build a phrase](#build-a-phrase) for the complete procedure.'
  musical_use: Use a short phrase to compare changes before expanding the arrangement.
  related:
