- id: sound-design
  title: Assigning Instruments to Channels
  audience: all
  summary: Select an output for each musical part.
  prose: '1. Press Grid `(3,8)` and select a channel.

    2. Open Channel tasks → Device.

    3. Select a MIDI device or installed n.b. player.

    4. For MIDI, set port and channel to match the instrument.

    5. Press K3 to apply.

    6. Assign a pattern and start playback to verify the output.


    Use separate channels for parts that need independent notes, masks or clock settings. Channel numbers
    have no reserved musical roles.'
  musical_use: Use Polyperc for bass or a plucked melody and Doubledecker for chords. Add Oilcan on a
    separate channel for percussion.
