- id: rhythm-section-design
  title: Creating a Rhythm Pattern
  audience: all
  summary: Enter trigs, then set note and velocity data.
  prose: '1. Press Grid `(5,8)` to open Pattern Trig.

    2. Select the required pattern.

    3. Press steps to add or remove trigs. Active steps light on the grid.

    4. Press Pattern again to open Note, then set relative notes.

    5. Press Pattern again to open Velocity, then set attack levels.

    6. Assign the pattern to a channel and start playback.


    Patterns have 64 steps. For algorithmic entry, prime a pattern, inspect the flashing preview, then
    paint it. A preview is not committed. Painting toggles overlaps with existing attacks off.'
  musical_use: For a 16-step pulse, use steps 1, 5, 9 and 13. Add step 15 for a pickup. For a 3–3–2 rhythm
    over eight steps, use 1, 4 and 7.
