      start from their stated starting projects; they do not load a replacement into your project.
  - title: Separate listening comparison
    text: Changing Harmony with Scale Slots uses the same upper relative degrees 0,0,0,1 and bass degrees
      0,4 to compare two C-major bars with two D-major bars. Its internal-player bass is deliberately
      set to velocity 60 and length 1/2, while the continuing MIDI course keeps inherited velocity 100
      and length 1. See the complete preparation in [Changing Harmony with Scale Slots](#tilting-harmony).
