- id: modulation-movement-and-interest
  title: Adding Parameter Variation
  audience: all
  summary: Extend the phrase with a lighter attack before the loop restarts.
  prose: 'Before starting: Use stopped channel 1, range 16, Rate /1, C major, pattern 1 assigned with
    attacks 1,5,9,13 and relative degrees 0,0,0,1. Set channel Note to X, Vel to 80 and Len to 1/2; step
    13 Vel is 50 and its Note is X. [Applying a Scale](#harmony-design) includes the note-mask clearance
    procedure.


    ### Add the late attack


    1. Tap Pattern (5,8) until Trig is shown; select pattern 1 at (1,1).

    2. Tap (15,4) to add step 15.

    3. Tap Pattern once to Note; tap (15,7) for degree 0.


    A C pickup falls halfway between the last beat and the next bar.


    ### Reduce the pickup level


    1. Select CH01, open Masks and select Vel.

    2. Hold step 15 and set 35 with E3.

    3. Release, play two bars and stop.


    The pickup is quieter than the main beats and the D ending. Probability and parameter slides are optional
    follow-up guides; this version remains deterministic.


    Resulting project: P1 attacks 1/5/9/13/15; degree 15=0; step 13Vel50; step 15Vel35; other velocities80;
    CH02 unchanged.'
  musical_use: Increase brightness or length on the final note. Apply probability to a quiet pickup while
    retaining the main attacks.
