- id: song-composition
  title: Arranging Song Slots
  audience: all
  summary: Alternate a sparse section and the full two-part phrase.
  prose: 'Before starting: Use one populated Song slot with two independently routed, audible channels
    and a 16-step loop. Slot 1 is selected; slots 2 and 3 are empty; playback is stopped. The example
    mutes CH01 while retaining CH02. [Make a piece](#learn) chapters 2–8 prepare the exact phrase and
    bass; an existing two-part loop with these conditions also works.


    ### Copy the complete section


    1. Open Song (6,8).

    2. Hold slot 1 (1,1), tap slot 2 (2,1), release slot 1.

    3. Select slot 2.


    Slot 2 stores the same phrase, bass and channel settings.


    ### Make the first section sparse


    1. Open Song (6,8); select slot 1 at (1,1).

    2. Tap Channel (3,8).

    3. Hold K1, tap channel 1 at (1,1), then release K1.

    4. Return to Song and select slot 2 at (2,1).

    5. Open Channel and check channel 1 is unmuted in this copy.


    Slot 1 contains bass only; slot 2 adds the upper phrase and pickup.


    ### Set the section boundary


    1. Open Song (6,8); select slot 1 at (1,1).

    2. Tap (2,7) to set Global length to 16 steps.

    3. Open Song tasks → Slot setup. Select Repeats with E2, set 1 with E3 and press K3 to apply.

    4. Return to Song; select slot 2 and repeat the Global length and Repeats settings.

    5. In Slot setup select Song mode, set On and press K3 to apply.

    6. Leave slot 3 empty and select slot 1.


    The contiguous group contains slots1 and2, one16-step pass each.


    ### Hear the arrangement


    Play four section passes and stop.


    Bass alone → bass and phrase → bass alone → bass and phrase. The highlighted Song slot changes at
    each boundary.


    Resulting project: Slot 1 CH01 muted/CH02 audible; slot 2 both channels audible. Global length 16;
    repeats1; Song modeOn; slot 3empty; selectedslot1; stopped.'
  musical_use: 'Create three sections: bass alone, bass with chords, then bass, chords and lead. Remove
    the lead for the final section.'
